    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44915" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐράξ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on one side, sideways</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆ δ᾽ εὐ. σὺν δουρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.251
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				15.541
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				920
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. πατάξ</span>, an exclamation in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1258
			</span></i>, to frighten away birds.</div>
